From f761e1a4bb760e2dfe2194c02aff42214c419d5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:17:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk/rm: Helios ICD interface, resource ids by IMPORT_RM,
 deviceLUID

What Conduit's Helios D3D11 UMD needs to run DXVK on NVK in a Windows
guest (Conduit guest/windows/docs/dxvk-on-nvk.md, stage S3):

- helios_icd_interface_v2, exported from vulkan_nouveau.dll: the
  backend-neutral table of helios_icd_interface.h (a verbatim copy of
  Conduit's guest/windows/protocol/include/helios_icd_interface.h).
  memory_res_id exports the dedicated memory of a 32 bpp image to a GEM
  object of the host render node (the export the scanout path already
  makes), creates one Venus holder context per process and asks the KMD
  for a resource id with HELIOS_ESCAPE_FOREIGN_RESOURCE IMPORT_RM,
  passing the image's layout (pitch or GB20x block-linear modifier, row
  pitch, offset). The id is released with the memory unless a WDDM
  allocation adopted it (transfer_ownership). scanout_present shows such
  an image through the KMD's foreign scanout source.
- HELIOS_STRUCTURE_TYPE_EXPORT_MEMORY_RESOURCE_INFO in
  vkAllocateMemory: shared, uncompressed, and the dedicated image's
  block-linear kind and tile mode recorded for the export.
- VkPhysicalDeviceIDProperties.deviceLUID = the Helios adapter's LUID
  (librmclient's crm_win_adapter_luid), deviceNodeMask 1.

Needs librmclient's crm_win_adapter_luid, crm_win_venus_ctx_create,
crm_win_foreign_caps, crm_win_import_rm and crm_win_release_blob; without
them (or with the KMD's IMPORT_RM gate closed) memory_res_id answers
VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT. NVK_HELIOS_RESID=0 turns resource ids off.
